WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.590
You wake up at seven in the morning

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.470
and pour yourself a glass of water.

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.350
Your roommate walks into the kitchen,

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:06.170
rubs his eyes,

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:06.710
and smiles.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:07.790
Morning.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:09.190
Did you sleep well,

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:09.570
he asks.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.050
Yeah, slept like a rock,

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:12.570
you reply.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.590
And right above your lips,

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.930
a bright crimson box flashes:

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:18.230
Lie.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.510
Rated eighty-four percent.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.590
You freeze.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.010
Your roommate looks at the

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.130
breakfast you made and says,

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.710
thanks, this tastes amazing.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.830
Floating right above his mouth in bold red letters:

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:31.830
Lie.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.010
He thinks it is cold and bland.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:36.190
For the next seven days,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.730
every spoken word in your world comes

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.290
with a verified truth rating.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.650
Green for absolute truth.

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:44.890
Bright crimson for deception.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:46.950
You think this power will give

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.050
you the ultimate advantage.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.830
You think you will finally know who to trust.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.270
Instead, by day seven,

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.310
you will understand the terrifying truth:

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.650
Honesty does not save relationships.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:00.170
Kindness does.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.090
And polite lies are the only reason

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.930
society has not burned to the ground.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.410
By noon on day one,

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.870
you are sitting in a team meeting at work.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.690
Your manager clicks to the next slide and says,

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.950
I really appreciate everyone's

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.590
extra hours on this launch.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.510
Crimson tag: Lie.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:20.930
He only cares about his quarterly bonus.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.250
A colleague leans over and whispers,

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.910
don't worry, your presentation was fantastic.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.210
Crimson tag: Lie.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.690
She did not listen to a single word.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:33.990
Psychologist Robert Feldman discovered that

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.170
in an ordinary ten-minute conversation,

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.010
the average human tells two to three lies.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.430
We do not do it because we are monsters.

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:44.010
We do it because radical honesty

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:45.710
is psychological warfare.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:48.110
Imagine if everyone said,

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:49.770
I am bored of talking to you.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.530
Your new haircut looks terrible.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.350
I only invited you because I felt obligated.

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:58.110
Civilization survives on tiny white lies

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:00.390
like an engine survives on motor oil.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.730
Without that oil,

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:03.990
human conversation grinds together

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.270
until the gears shatter.

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:07.430
By the end of your second day,

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.870
you are terrified to speak.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.370
Because every time someone is nice to you,

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.350
the glowing red badge tells you:

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.810
They are only trying to survive the interaction.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.730
By day four,

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:21.110
the small white lies stop bothering you.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.830
It is the deeper lies that begin to tear you apart.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:27.930
You meet your closest friend for coffee.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:31.170
You ask him how he has been doing since his breakup.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:33.290
He smiles and says,

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.250
honestly, I am completely over it.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.190
I feel freer than ever.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.010
Above his chest,

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.290
a soft red glow pulses:

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:43.390
Lie.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.150
He cries himself to sleep every night.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:49.370
Here, the crimson tag is not malice.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:50.530
It is shame.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.170
Humans lie to hide their bleeding wounds.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.510
We lie so our friends will not

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.330
see how fragile we really are.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.550
Then comes the real shock.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:02.150
You ask him,

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:03.390
are we good?

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.530
You felt distant lately.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.170
He pauses, looks at the table,

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:11.530
and says: I was envious of your promotion.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.750
And I hated myself for feeling that way.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:16.370
Above his words,

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:17.990
there is no red tag.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.310
A soft emerald light illuminates the air:

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:23.910
Truth.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.150
One hundred percent.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.210
It hits you like a physical shock.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:30.950
Hearing an ugly truth feels ten times more

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.870
loving than hearing a beautiful lie.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.710
Because for the first time in your life,

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.710
you are meeting a human being without armor.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.170
On the evening of day six,

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.170
you walk back to your apartment in complete silence.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.270
You realize that you have spent

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:48.330
five days judging the world.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.090
You analyzed your boss.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:51.630
You tested your friends.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.410
You graded every stranger on the subway.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.070
So you walk into your bathroom.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:58.530
You lock the door.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.190
And you look straight into your own reflection.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.270
I am happy with where I am in life,

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.030
you whisper.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:07.510
Crimson flash: Lie.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.070
I do not care what people think of me.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:12.250
Crimson flash: Lie.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.430
I have forgiven everyone who hurt me.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.170
A violent red pulse:

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:18.210
Lie.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.630
The tears start running down your cheeks.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.510
The most dangerous deceiver in your life

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.610
was never your coworker or your partner.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:26.770
It was you.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.090
We tell ourselves comfortable fairy tales so

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.070
we do not have to face our fear of failure,

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.590
our grief, and our loneliness.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.730
You stare into the mirror and finally say the

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:39.190
one thing you have avoided for ten years:

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.730
I am terrified of being alone.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:43.750
And I am trying my best.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:45.950
For the first time all week,

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:47.350
the crimson vanishes.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:51.130
A deep, tranquil green envelops the glass:

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:52.230
Truth.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:53.530
Absolute.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:56.450
Midnight arrives on the seventh day.

00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:59.990
The glowing tags fade into the quiet night air.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.090
Over the last six weeks,

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:05.150
you have experienced every impossible power:

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.650
You saw the salaries of every neighbor

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.070
and realized wealth buys comfort,

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:10.890
not peace.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.690
You saw the karma scores and learned

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:15.950
that morality is an inward discipline,

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.230
not a public spectacle.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:20.270
You heard what people whispered behind your back

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.550
and found the freedom of not needing applause.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.250
You tasted infinite save points and

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.070
discovered that life's beauty exists

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:30.390
only because mistakes are permanent.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.450
You saw the countdown clocks of mortality

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.990
and learned that our limited time is

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.910
what makes every moment sacred.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.190
And now, seeing every lie has

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.690
taught you the ultimate lesson:

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.770
Truth without empathy is cruelty.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:48.110
And honesty without vulnerability

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:49.610
is just another weapon.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.490
You step outside onto the morning sidewalk.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.230
The barista hands you your cup and says,

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.370
have a wonderful day.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:58.350
There is no green tag.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.850
There is no red tag.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.710
Just two strangers on a spinning rock,

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.650
trying to be kind to each other.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:06.810
You smile back at her,

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:08.270
take a sip of hot coffee,

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:10.510
and whisper: Thank you.

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:11.950
And this time,

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.090
in your heart,

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.670
you know it is the absolute truth.
